              "“Right now, China is feeling the blow really of our tariffs, and I think that that’s an appropriate place for us to have taken the relationship given the amount of stuff that they were stealing from us,” said White House Council of Economic Advisers chairman Kevin Hassett said in an interview with CNN’s Poppy Harlow last week",
              "While the Trump administration’s hardline stance has failed to produce a comprehensive trade agreement so far, the two sides reached a truce in early December after Chinese President Xi Jinping met with Trump at the G20 summit in Buenos Aires.\n\nTrump agreed to maintain 10% tariffs on $200 billion worth of Chinese goods, and not raise them to 25% “at this time” ahead of a January 1 deadline",
